  abstract = {The present study aims to investigate the cognate and gender congruency effects in Bulgarian-English proficient bilinguals using a visual word translation task. The results of two experiments confirm the pattern generally observed in the area: we have found a strong cognate effect present in both translation directions (from the dominant L1 into nondominant L2 and vice versa). In addition, we have obtained a gender congruency effect which suggests that bilinguals use gender information of their native language during translation.},
